Per-state coverage (web AIFeedbackQueueTriage -> native TriageSurface), all asserted in ModelTest + rendered by @Preview:
  loading  -> Working (streaming, no delta)            [streamingWithoutTextIsWorking ; @Preview Working]
  content  -> Live (partial) / Ready (done, fresh)     [streamingWithTextIsLive, doneWithTextIsReady* ; @Preview Live/Ready]
  empty    -> Resting (idle) / Empty (done, blank)     [restingReflectsCanStart, doneBlankIsEmpty ; @Preview Resting/Empty]
  error    -> Failed(offline?) with retry              [failed*WithoutLastKnown* ; @Preview Error]
  stale    -> Ready(stale=true) stale chip             [doneWithTextIsReadyAndStaleBeyondWindow ; @Preview Stale]
  offline  -> Cached(offline=true) cached + offline chip[failedNetworkWithLastKnownIsOfflineCached ; @Preview Offline]
  gate-off -> Hidden (web withAiFeature -> null)        [gateOffHidesSurface ; @Preview Hidden]
  10 @Preview entry points exercise each rendered state.

A11y: headerAccessibilityLabel merges title+badge+description (mergeDescendants TalkBack node); outputAccessibilityLabel
  drives a Polite live-region per state; both unit-tested (headerLabelMerges..., outputLabelCoversEveryAnnouncedSurface,
  outputLabelIsAbsentForRestingAndHidden). Suggest/Retry buttons carry localized accessible labels; reduce-motion respected
  (rememberReducedMotion gates the shimmer). minSdk=26.

Telemetry (P1/S11): onViewOpened() emits view.opened {slug=AIFeedbackQueueTriage} at most once (viewOpenedEmitsOnceWithSlug);
  suggest() emits aiFeedbackTriage.suggest carrying NO feedback_id / text (suggestEmitsDiagnosticWithoutPii).

Parity-with-honesty divergences:
  - useUpdateFeedback is NOT bound: the web source header is explicit that this advisor is propose-only and never
    calls useUpdateFeedback (the manual triage controls remain the sole write path). The prompt data-source list
    names it, but the web source is THE spec, so the surface binds only useAiStream + i18n. Documented, not narrowed.
  - stale -> manual re-suggest (not auto-refresh): re-running an LLM draft is billable, so the stale surface invites
    an explicit re-suggest (sibling-consistent with AIChargingDiagnosis 0011).

i18n (P1/S10) — necessary catalog completion, fully disclosed:
  The web source uses feedbackTriage.aiAdvisor.{title,description,button,badge}. Unlike every predecessor (whose keys
  pre-existed in the canonical web catalog), these were ABSENT everywhere (web shipped inline t() defaults only). Per
  ADR-014 (canonical = web/src/i18n/*.json; native strings.xml is GENERATED, never hand-edited) I added the 4 keys to
  web/src/i18n/en.json and materialized the Android base resource via the sanctioned generator (gen-i18n.ts), then
  captured the byte-exact generated <string> lines and reverted the unrelated bulk so this surface PR stays
  Android-scoped (en.json + values/strings.xml only).
  Pre-existing repo-wide i18n drift (NOT introduced here): gen-i18n.ps1 -Check was already RED before this change
  (11 files; web 7902 entries vs committed 7779 ~= 123 entries from other features awaiting the periodic regen).
  ar/he are placeholder locales (English fallback auto-materialized), so no per-locale edit is needed. Full
  multi-platform regeneration (catalog/ar/he/windows/apple) is the P1/S10 i18n artifact batch scope; this surface
  adds only its 4 canonical keys + the Android base resource required to compile and render. The gate above does not
  run the i18n -Check, so no green is claimed for it.

